1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Your road. In view.
Speed limits, Dashcam and street imagery with YouSpeed.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Mount it. Set it up.
Before driving, secure the phone and keep the rear camera unobstructed.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Choose your mounting position
Open Settings. Choose portrait or the matching landscape position.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Align the camera before driving
Tap the viewfinder. Align the horizon and lane guides, then Save.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Enable camera recognition
Allow camera access. Install regional data in Data Manager, then enable sign recognition.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Start your drive recording
Tap the red recorder. Dashcam and your enabled camera features start together.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Keep the drive
Real iPhone Dashcam footage, saved locally for playback and sharing.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Stop. Save. Play.
Tap the recorder again to stop. Open Gallery → Videos to replay or share.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Choose when pictures are captured
Enable Capture pictures. Set a distance or time interval; photos stay on your device.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
See the places you pass
After your drive, open Gallery → Pictures. Review photos and mark favourites.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Review first. Share when ready.
Select your pictures, then tap Upload. Connect a Panoramax account in Settings first.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Camera-based speed limits
Example camera result: the eye marks a camera-supplied limit. A regional model is required.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
More than speed limits
Example recognition display: additional road signs appear beside the limit.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Ready for the road
Configure while parked. Keep your attention on the road and follow posted signs.
